 {"id":"fabro-5e09","title":"Develop planner: pick only seeds assigned to fabro (sd ready --assignee fabro) — deterministic line/user ownership split","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T12:16:32.837Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T12:26:40.545Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"USER CORRECTION 2026-09-07 (governance): the LINE implements only the MECHANISM; WHICH seeds belong to the line is a USER decision, never a bulk heuristic run by the line itself.\n\nMECHANISM (line implements): (1) develop planner prompt (.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md) candidate source becomes 'sd ready --assignee fabro --limit 200' — CLI pre-filters, the LLM never sees seeds not assigned to fabro (data-level determinism); (2) goal fast-path honors a named seed id ONLY when assignee is fabro; (3) claim step: 'sd update <id> --status in_progress --assignee fabro'; (4) Tracker-empty on the FILTERED view = legitimate end of work (park), not a broken tracker — FAIL-CLOSED: while the backlog is unassigned the line does nothing rather than something; (5) docs/agents/issue-tracker.md documents the convention: assignee is the ownership switch; filers assign at creation; the user can reassign/unassign anytime as veto.\n\nOWNERSHIP (user decides, NOT this seed's implementer): the existing backlog assignment list is prepared by the agent as a proposal, reviewed and approved by the USER in chat (or the pending grill session), then applied from the user side. NO bulk-assign by the develop run. The sentinel pair (fabro-919b/fabro-80cc) stays in place until the mechanism lands AND the user has curated the backlog; retiring it is part of the user-approved migration, not this implementation.\n\nAcceptance: planner prompt ships the filtered command; a user-assigned open seed never appears in a develop run's candidates; empty filtered view parks; docs updated; ownership list untouched by the implementer.","labels":["workflows","revision"]}
